course: dictionary
lesson: 12377
title: Crushingly and strong feelings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Crushingly comes from crush, which means to squeeze something so hard it breaks or flattens. When a result is crushing, it squashes your hopes flat. «The home team was crushingly defeated, losing nine goals to none.» The word crushingly tells you the defeat was very big, not just a small loss.
explain: Crushingly is an adverb: it tells you how strong something is, and it often comes before an adjective. «The film was crushingly boring.» Here crushingly comes before boring, and it means extremely boring. Check it by swapping in extremely: «The film was extremely boring» still makes sense, so you have found its meaning.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Defeated, nine goals to none, and disappointing all show something bad and very strong. So crushingly means very strongly or overwhelmingly. It is not about something being squashed in a literal way.
fact: Crushingly is an adverb, a word that describes how something happens or how strong something is.
fact: «Crushingly» means very strongly, or in a way that feels overwhelming.
fact: Before an adjective, «crushingly» means extremely, as in «crushingly boring».
fact: «Crushingly» comes from «crush», which means to squeeze or press flat.
fact: Sports reports often use «crushingly defeated» to show a team lost by a big margin.
exercise: «The team was crushingly defeated, losing nine goals to none.» What does crushingly mean here? | Very quietly | Only just | *By a very big margin | Slowly and carefully
exercise: «The film was crushingly boring.» Which word means the same as crushingly here? | Sometimes | Slightly | *Extremely | Quickly
exercise: Pick the word that fits best: The news was ___ disappointing for the children. | Ancient | Luminous | Barely | *Crushingly
test: «The result was crushingly disappointing for the fans.» What does crushingly mean here? | Very quietly | *Very strongly, so the fans felt very let down | Just a little | Slowly and carefully
test: Which word could replace crushingly in «crushingly obvious»? | *Extremely | Slowly | Happily | Barely
exam: Which sentence uses crushingly to mean extremely? | She crushed the paper into a ball | The dog barked crushingly loudly at the post | *The exam was crushingly hard for everyone | The lamp was crushed by the heavy door
